      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could we check `policer_lock()` before releasing the current attachment or storing the new index, and propagate a failure to the caller? Attaching nonexistent index 0 is currently accepted despite the failed lock. If a policer is then allocated at index 0, removing the attachment unlocks its zero reference count and aborts debug VPP. This reproduced under debug ASAN for both IPv4 and IPv6. A rejected replacement should preserve the existing attachment and its reference.",
