      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is not related to this patch, the behavior you describe was already there when disabling policing on this path. `Removal now clears the policer index to ~0`, this was always the case but not enforce in the function. Before `ip6_punt_policer_add_del()` was always called with `~0` as policer index when `is_add \u003d\u003d false`.\n\nIt seems that it should be addressed in the punt node, dropping packets that have a policer index that does not exist.",
